#: ../../source/arch_README.md:16
msgid ""
"This module is used by [WebTorrent Desktop](http://webtorrent.io/desktop)"
" to determine if the user is on a 32-bit vs. 64-bit operating system to "
"offer the right app installer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arch_README.md:20
msgid ""
"In Node.js, the `os.arch()` method (and `process.arch` property) returns "
"a string identifying the operating system CPU architecture **for which "
"the Node.js binary was compiled**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arch_README.md:24
msgid ""
"This is not the same as the **operating system CPU architecture**. For "
"example, you can run Node.js 32-bit on a 64-bit OS. In that situation, "
"`os.arch()` will return a misleading 'x86' (32-bit) value, instead of "
"'x64' (64-bit)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arch_README.md:28
msgid "Use this package to get the actual operating system CPU architecture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arch_README.md:30
msgid "**BONUS: This package works in the browser too.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arch_README.md:32
msgid "install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arch_README.md:38
msgid "usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arch_README.md:45
msgid ""
"In the browser, there is no spec that defines where this information "
"lives, so we check all known locations including `navigator.userAgent`, "
"`navigator.platform`, and `navigator.cpuClass` to make a best guess."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arch_README.md:49
msgid ""
"If there is no *affirmative indication* that the architecture is 64-bit, "
"then 32-bit will be assumed. This makes this package perfect for "
"determining what installer executable to offer to desktop app users. If "
"there is ambiguity, then the user will get the 32-bit installer, which "
"will work fine even for a user with a 64-bit OS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arch_README.md:55
msgid "For reference, `x64` means 64-bit and `x86` means 32-bit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arch_README.md:57
msgid "Here is some history behind these naming conventions:"
